/* The handoff's mutation strip:
 *
 *     background: linear-gradient(100deg, #fdf0d0, #f9e0a8);
 *     border-radius: 14px; padding: 9px 11px;
 *     box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 1px rgba(196,150,45,.28);
 *     <24px white disc, glow 2s>  <11px copy in #7a5b12>
 *
 * THE GRADIENT IS A TEXTURE, like the CTA's, because USS has none (Theme.uss
 * header item 1). amber-ramp.png is 64x2 rather than 2x64 - the handoff's
 * angle is 100deg, ten degrees off horizontal, so the ramp runs across the
 * strip rather than down it. generate-textures.py has the three ramps and
 * their angles together.
 *
 * THE INSET RING IS A REAL BORDER, because USS has no inset box-shadow
 * either - the same substitution `.option--selected` makes in Theme.uss. The
 * handoff's is #c4962d at 28%, which composites over its own #f9e0a8 to
 * about #eacb85; --amber is one step stronger than that and is the token
 * this family already has. A strip that has to read as rarer than everything
 * around it is the wrong place to spend a step of contrast.
 *
 * THE FILL AND THE RADIUS AND THE PADDING ARE `.panel-amber`'s, not this
 * sheet's. Its radius is --radius-row (14px), which is the handoff's number
 * exactly, and its padding is --space-3 against the handoff's 9/11 - inside
 * the band the README gives for a row. Setting them again here would put two
 * single-class rules from two sheets on the same properties, which is the
 * order-dependence every override in this task is written to avoid.
 *
 * THE ANIMATION IS NOT REPRODUCED. The handoff pulses the disc on a 2s
 * `glow`; Motion.uss owns this project's transitions and has no keyframe
 * vocabulary, and a still capture is the phase's verification. Named here
 * so it reads as a decision rather than an oversight.
 */
.mutation-banner {
    flex-direction: row;
    align-items: center;
    flex-shrink: 0;
    background-image: url("project:///Assets/UI/Art/amber-ramp.png");
    -unity-background-scale-mode: stretch-to-fill;
    border-width: 1px;
    border-color: var(--amber);
    margin-top: 11px;
}

/* 12px is half of 24 - a square element, so both axes clamp alike and this
 * is a true circle (Theme.uss header item 4). */
.mutation-banner__disc {
    width: 24px;
    height: 24px;
    border-radius: 12px;
    background-color: var(--surface);
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    flex-shrink: 0;
    margin-right: var(--space-2);
}

/* TWO CLASSES, to beat icons.uss's `.icon` (19px, --mute-soft) without
 * depending on which sheet the panel applies last. The handoff draws this
 * mark at 12px in the 24px disc, in a deep amber that is neither the warning
 * brown nor the tint - Tokens.uss's --amber-bright-deep note has the two
 * measurements that ruled both out. */
.mutation-banner .mutation-banner__spark {
    width: 12px;
    height: 12px;
    -unity-background-image-tint-color: var(--amber-bright-deep);
}

/* --amber-text comes from `.t-warn`. `white-space: normal` so a sentence
 * wraps rather than running off the strip: the copy is authored by the
 * server and this component cannot know its length, which is exactly the
 * mistake `.screen-scaffold__footer-note` records making once. */
.mutation-banner__text {
    flex-grow: 1;
    flex-shrink: 1;
    white-space: normal;
    font-size: var(--text-secondary);
}
